# M6 4a (slice 345; Codex CODEX-OPUS-345-4A-REPLY-20261110T041147Z-01 item 1): `a := value`, the named actual of
# 2026-11-07, is no actual since 4a -- the translation refuses it before any actual is computed, with no fallback to the
# named supply and none to a positional value; the named actual is written `a: value` (named_assign_actuals).
fn: tst (int: c 3; int: a 2) int
    return: c * 10 + a
end: tst
int: code 7
if: tst(a := 5) != 35
    code: 81
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
